VG.registerBibleChapters("genesis", [
{n:46, name:"The Journey to Egypt", seal:{ref:"Genesis 46:3",verse:"And he said, I am God, the God of thy father: fear not to go down into Egypt; for I will there make of thee a great nation:"}, facts:["Did you know that seventy souls of the house of Jacob went down into Egypt, the small beginning of the great nation God had promised?","Did you know that when Jacob saw Joseph alive in Goshen, he said, Now let me die, since I have seen thy face, because thou art yet alive?","Did you know the Egyptians counted every shepherd an abomination, which is why Joseph settled his family apart in the land of Goshen?"], questions:[
{q:"At which place did Jacob stop to offer sacrifices on his way down to Egypt?",options:["Beersheba","Hebron","Bethel","Shechem"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:1",verse:"And Israel took his journey with all that he had, and came to Beer-sheba, and offered sacrifices unto the God of his father Isaac.",insight:"Before entering Egypt, Jacob stopped at Beersheba to worship the God of his father Isaac. New seasons are best entered with old faithfulness."},
{q:"How did God speak to Jacob at Beersheba?",options:["In the visions of the night","Through a burning bush","By a voice from the clouds","In a dream of a ladder"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:2",verse:"And God spake unto Israel in the visions of the night, and said, Jacob, Jacob. And he said, Here am I.",insight:"God called Jacob by name twice in the night, and Jacob answered, Here am I. God still speaks personally in dark hours to those who listen."},
{q:"What did God tell Jacob not to fear?",options:["Going down into Egypt","The famine in Canaan","The journey through the desert","Pharaoh's power"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:3",verse:"And he said, I am God, the God of thy father: fear not to go down into Egypt; for I will there make of thee a great nation:",insight:"The command not to fear came with a promise attached. Courage grows where God's promise is clear."},
{q:"What did God promise to make of Jacob in Egypt?",options:["A great nation","A wealthy household","A royal priesthood","A fortified city"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:3",verse:"And he said, I am God, the God of thy father: fear not to go down into Egypt; for I will there make of thee a great nation:",insight:"Egypt looked like exile, but God called it the nursery of a nation. What feels like displacement may be preparation."},
{q:"According to God's promise, whose hand would be upon Jacob's eyes at his death?",options:["Joseph's","Judah's","Reuben's","Benjamin's"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:4",verse:"I will go down with thee into Egypt; and I will also surely bring thee up again: and Joseph shall put his hand upon thine eyes.",insight:"God promised Jacob that Joseph, long thought dead, would close his eyes. Restoration can reach into our very last moments."},
{q:"How did the sons of Israel carry Jacob out of Beersheba?",options:["In the wagons Pharaoh had sent","On camels loaded with goods","In litters borne by servants","On the shoulders of his sons"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:5",verse:"And Jacob rose up from Beer-sheba: and the sons of Israel carried Jacob their father, and their little ones, and their wives, in the wagons which Pharaoh had sent to carry him.",insight:"Pharaoh's wagons carried the old patriarch south. God often provides the practical means for the journey He commands."},
{q:"Who is named as Jacob's firstborn?",options:["Reuben","Judah","Joseph","Simeon"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:8",verse:"And these are the names of the children of Israel, which came into Egypt, Jacob and his sons: Reuben, Jacob’s firstborn.",insight:"The record begins with Reuben, the firstborn, setting the birth order that shaped the tribes. God works through real families with real histories."},
{q:"Which son of Simeon was born of a Canaanitish woman?",options:["Shaul","Jemuel","Jamin","Zohar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:10",verse:"And the sons of Simeon; Jemuel, and Jamin, and Ohad, and Jachin, and Zohar, and Shaul the son of a Canaanitish woman.",insight:"Shaul's mother is named honestly in the record. Scripture does not hide mixed or complicated family lines."},
{q:"Which three are named as the sons of Levi?",options:["Gershon, Kohath, and Merari","Amram, Izhar, and Hebron","Libni, Shimei, and Uzziel","Aaron, Moses, and Miriam"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:11",verse:"And the sons of Levi; Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.",insight:"From Levi's three sons would come the priests and the Levites. Small family records carry large redemptive futures."},
{q:"Which two sons of Judah died in the land of Canaan?",options:["Er and Onan","Pharez and Zerah","Shelah and Hezron","Hamul and Carmi"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:12",verse:"And the sons of Judah; Er, and Onan, and Shelah, and Pharez, and Zarah: but Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan. And the sons of Pharez were Hezron and Hamul.",insight:"Er and Onan died before the journey, yet Judah's line continued through Pharez. God's purposes outlive individual failures."},
{q:"How many souls are reckoned to Leah's line?",options:["Thirty and three","Thirty and six","Forty and four","Twenty and eight"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:15",verse:"These be the sons of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob in Padan-aram, with his daughter Dinah: all the souls of his sons and his daughters were thirty and three.",insight:"Thirty-three souls are counted to Leah, the unloved wife who became the mother of Judah. God honors those the world overlooks."},
{q:"Which tribe's record names a woman, Serah, among its members?",options:["Asher","Gad","Dan","Naphtali"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:17",verse:"And the sons of Asher; Jimnah, and Ishuah, and Isui, and Beriah, and Serah their sister: and the sons of Beriah; Heber, and Malchiel.",insight:"Serah, daughter of Asher, is preserved by name in a list of sons. Every person matters enough to God to be recorded."},
{q:"What were the names of Joseph's two sons born in Egypt?",options:["Manasseh and Ephraim","Gershon and Eliezer","Shechem and Shiloh","Machir and Gilead"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:20",verse:"And unto Joseph in the land of Egypt were born Manasseh and Ephraim, which Asenath the daughter of Poti-pherah priest of On bare unto him.",insight:"Manasseh and Ephraim were born in Egypt yet counted in Israel. God's people can grow even in foreign soil."},
{q:"Who was the mother of Manasseh and Ephraim?",options:["Asenath, daughter of Potipherah, priest of On","A daughter of Pharaoh's house","A Canaanitish woman of Shechem","A handmaid of Rachel's house"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:20",verse:"And unto Joseph in the land of Egypt were born Manasseh and Ephraim, which Asenath the daughter of Poti-pherah priest of On bare unto him.",insight:"Asenath, an Egyptian priest's daughter, became the mother of two tribes. Grace weaves outsiders into the covenant story."},
{q:"How many souls belonged to Rachel's line?",options:["Fourteen","Sixteen","Seven","Thirty and three"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:22",verse:"These are the sons of Rachel, which were born to Jacob: all the souls were fourteen.",insight:"Fourteen souls came through Rachel, the beloved wife. Love remembered her, and so did the record."},
{q:"How many souls came down with Jacob into Egypt, besides his sons' wives?",options:["Threescore and six","Threescore and ten","Seventy and seven","Fifty and two"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:26",verse:"All the souls that came with Jacob into Egypt, which came out of his loins, besides Jacob’s sons’ wives, all the souls were threescore and six;",insight:"Sixty-six came out of Jacob's loins, not counting the wives. God counts His people precisely; none are lost in the crowd."},
{q:"What was the total number of the house of Jacob that came into Egypt?",options:["Threescore and ten","Threescore and six","Seventy and five","Sixty and four"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:27",verse:"And the sons of Joseph, which were born him in Egypt, were two souls: all the souls of the house of Jacob, which came into Egypt, were threescore and ten.",insight:"Seventy souls went down, a small family with a huge promise. Nations begin as households that trust God."},
{q:"Whom did Jacob send ahead to direct the way to Goshen?",options:["Judah","Reuben","Simeon","Levi"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:28",verse:"And he sent Judah before him unto Joseph, to direct his face unto Goshen; and they came into the land of Goshen.",insight:"Judah went before to prepare the way, a quiet preview of his tribe's leading role. Leaders go first so others can follow."},
{q:"What did Joseph do when he met his father in Goshen?",options:["Fell on his neck and wept a good while","Bow down to the earth seven times","Presented him to Pharaoh at once","Offered sacrifices of thanksgiving"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:29",verse:"And Joseph made ready his chariot, and went up to meet Israel his father, to Goshen, and presented himself unto him; and he fell on his neck, and wept on his neck a good while.",insight:"After long years apart, Joseph wept on his father's neck a good while. Reconciliation is worth the tears it costs."},
{q:"Why did Joseph want his family settled apart in the land of Goshen?",options:["For every shepherd was an abomination unto the Egyptians","Because Goshen had the richest soil in Egypt","So Pharaoh could tax their flocks more easily","To keep them near the border for escape"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 46:34",verse:"That ye shall say, Thy servants’ trade hath been about cattle from our youth even until now, both we, and also our fathers: that ye may dwell in the land of Goshen; for every shepherd is an abomination unto the Egyptians.",insight:"Egypt despised shepherds, so God used that contempt to keep Israel distinct. Sometimes rejection is protection in disguise."}
]},
{n:47, name:"Settled in Goshen", seal:{ref:"Genesis 47:27",verse:"And Israel dwelt in the land of Egypt, in the country of Goshen; and they had possessions therein, and grew, and multiplied exceedingly."}, facts:["Did you know Jacob was 130 years old when he stood before Pharaoh, and he described his life as a pilgrimage of few and evil days?","Did you know Joseph set the fifth part of the harvest for Pharaoh, and it became law in Egypt unto this day?","Did you know Jacob lived seventeen years in Egypt, so his whole age was 147 years?"], questions:[
{q:"How many of his brothers did Joseph present before Pharaoh?",options:["Five men","Seven men","Three men","Twelve men"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:2",verse:"And he took some of his brethren, even five men, and presented them unto Pharaoh.",insight:"Joseph chose five brothers to stand before Pharaoh. Representation matters; a few can speak for the many."},
{q:"What did the brothers tell Pharaoh their occupation was?",options:["Shepherds","Herdsmen of camels","Traders in spices","Keepers of vineyards"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:3",verse:"And Pharaoh said unto his brethren, What is your occupation? And they said unto Pharaoh, Thy servants are shepherds, both we, and also our fathers.",insight:"They answered honestly, shepherds like their fathers. Integrity about who you are opens doors God has prepared."},
{q:"Why had Jacob's family come to sojourn in Egypt?",options:["The famine was sore and they had no pasture for their flocks","Pharaoh had invited them to a royal feast","War had driven them from Canaan","They sought to buy land for burial"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:4",verse:"They said moreover unto Pharaoh, For to sojourn in the land are we come; for thy servants have no pasture for their flocks; for the famine is sore in the land of Canaan: now therefore, we pray thee, let thy servants dwell in the land of Goshen.",insight:"Need drove them to Egypt, but God had gone before them. Our necessities often walk roads grace already paved."},
{q:"In which land did Pharaoh tell Joseph to settle his family?",options:["The land of Goshen","The field of Zoan","The plain of Memphis","The region of Thebes"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:6",verse:"The land of Egypt is before thee; in the best of the land make thy father and brethren to dwell; in the land of Goshen let them dwell: and if thou knowest any men of activity among them, then make them rulers over my cattle.",insight:"Pharaoh gave them Goshen, the best of the land. God can turn a pagan king's favor into His people's provision."},
{q:"What office did Pharaoh offer to capable men among Jacob's sons?",options:["Rulers over his cattle","Captains of his guard","Keepers of his storehouses","Scribes of his court"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:6",verse:"The land of Egypt is before thee; in the best of the land make thy father and brethren to dwell; in the land of Goshen let them dwell: and if thou knowest any men of activity among them, then make them rulers over my cattle.",insight:"Skill with livestock earned a place in Pharaoh's service. Excellence in ordinary work is noticed in high places."},
{q:"What did Jacob do when Joseph set him before Pharaoh?",options:["Blessed Pharaoh","Bow down to the ground","Offered him gifts of Canaan","Swore allegiance to Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:7",verse:"And Joseph brought in Jacob his father, and set him before Pharaoh: and Jacob blessed Pharaoh.",insight:"The old shepherd blessed the mightiest king on earth. Those who walk with God carry blessing into every palace."},
{q:"What question did Pharaoh ask Jacob?",options:["How old art thou?","Whence comest thou?","What is thy god?","How many are thy sons?"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:8",verse:"And Pharaoh said unto Jacob, How old art thou?",insight:"Pharaoh asked about Jacob's age, sensing a life of weight. A long life with God commands respect even from kings."},
{q:"How old did Jacob say he was when he stood before Pharaoh?",options:["An hundred and thirty years","An hundred and twenty years","An hundred and forty years","Ninety and nine years"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:9",verse:"And Jacob said unto Pharaoh, The days of the years of my pilgrimage are an hundred and thirty years: few and evil have the days of the years of my life been, and have not attained unto the days of the years of the life of my fathers in the days of their pilgrimage.",insight:"At 130, Jacob measured his years as pilgrimage, not possession. Life is a journey, and he knew the destination."},
{q:"How did Jacob describe the days of his life to Pharaoh?",options:["Few and evil","Long and peaceful","Rich and full","Calm and quiet"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:9",verse:"And Jacob said unto Pharaoh, The days of the years of my pilgrimage are an hundred and thirty years: few and evil have the days of the years of my life been, and have not attained unto the days of the years of the life of my fathers in the days of their pilgrimage.",insight:"Jacob called his days few and evil beside his fathers'. Honest sorrow can live alongside unshaken faith."},
{q:"By what name is the district called where Joseph settled his family?",options:["The land of Rameses","The city of On","The field of Zoan","The town of Pithom"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:11",verse:"And Joseph placed his father and his brethren, and gave them a possession in the land of Egypt, in the best of the land, in the land of Rameses, as Pharaoh had commanded.",insight:"Rameses, in the best of the land, became Israel's home. God plants His people where they can grow."},
{q:"Who nourished all his father's household with bread during the famine?",options:["Joseph","Pharaoh","Judah","The priests of On"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:12",verse:"And Joseph nourished his father, and his brethren, and all his father’s household, with bread, according to their families.",insight:"Joseph fed his father's whole household according to their families. The one once thrown in a pit became the family's bread."},
{q:"What did Joseph do with the money paid for corn?",options:["Brought it into Pharaoh's house","Distributed it to the poor","Stored it in his own barns","Sent it back to Canaan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:14",verse:"And Joseph gathered up all the money that was found in the land of Egypt, and in the land of Canaan, for the corn which they bought: and Joseph brought the money into Pharaoh’s house.",insight:"Every coin went to Pharaoh's house; Joseph handled wealth without skimming. Faithfulness in administration is a quiet virtue."},
{q:"When the people's money failed, what did Joseph accept for bread?",options:["Their cattle","Their garments","Their weapons","Their household goods"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:16",verse:"And Joseph said, Give your cattle; and I will give you for your cattle, if money fail.",insight:"Cattle bought bread for a year. Joseph met desperate need with practical mercy, stage by stage."},
{q:"After their cattle were gone, what did the Egyptians say was all they had left?",options:["Their bodies and their lands","Their houses and their gold","Their children and their wives","Their tools and their seed"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:18",verse:"When that year was ended, they came unto him the second year, and said unto him, We will not hide it from my lord, how that our money is spent; my lord also hath our herds of cattle; there is not ought left in the sight of my lord, but our bodies, and our lands:",insight:"They came with nothing left but bodies and lands, and Joseph still gave seed. Mercy finds a way when resources run out."},
{q:"What did Joseph buy for Pharaoh with the people's surrender?",options:["All the land of Egypt","The city of Memphis","The temple treasures","The Nile fleet"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:20",verse:"And Joseph bought all the land of Egypt for Pharaoh; for the Egyptians sold every man his field, because the famine prevailed over them: so the land became Pharaoh’s.",insight:"The whole land became Pharaoh's through Joseph's administration. Wisdom in crisis reshapes nations."},
{q:"Whose land did Joseph NOT buy for Pharaoh?",options:["The priests'","The soldiers'","The merchants'","The shepherds'"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:22",verse:"Only the land of the priests bought he not; for the priests had a portion assigned them of Pharaoh, and did eat their portion which Pharaoh gave them: wherefore they sold not their lands.",insight:"The priests kept their portion from Pharaoh. Even in sweeping change, some boundaries are honored."},
{q:"What portion of the harvest did Joseph set apart for Pharaoh?",options:["The fifth part","The tenth part","The third part","The half"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:24",verse:"And it shall come to pass in the increase, that ye shall give the fifth part unto Pharaoh, and four parts shall be your own, for seed of the field, and for your food, and for them of your households, and for food for your little ones.",insight:"One fifth for Pharaoh, four fifths for the people, with seed for sowing. Joseph's tax left the farmers able to live and plant again."},
{q:"What did the people say Joseph had done for them?",options:["Thou hast saved our lives","Thou hast made us rich","Thou hast freed our children","Thou hast given us land"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:25",verse:"And they said, Thou hast saved our lives: let us find grace in the sight of my lord, and we will be Pharaoh’s servants.",insight:"They confessed, Thou hast saved our lives, and became willing servants. Gratitude turns rescue into loyalty."},
{q:"How many years did Jacob live in Egypt?",options:["Seventeen years","Twenty-two years","Thirty years","Seven years"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:28",verse:"And Jacob lived in the land of Egypt seventeen years: so the whole age of Jacob was an hundred forty and seven years.",insight:"Seventeen years in Egypt closed a 147-year life. The final chapter can be the most fruitful of all."},
{q:"Where did Jacob ask Joseph NOT to bury him?",options:["In Egypt","In the cave of Machpelah","In the land of Goshen","In the city of Rameses"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 47:29",verse:"And the time drew nigh that Israel must die: and he called his son Joseph, and said unto him, If now I have found grace in thy sight, put, I pray thee, thy hand under my thigh, and deal kindly and truly with me; bury me not, I pray thee, in Egypt:",insight:"Bury me not in Egypt, he pleaded. Jacob's heart stayed fixed on the promised land, even in death."}
]},
{n:48, name:"Ephraim and Manasseh Blessed", seal:{ref:"Genesis 48:16",verse:"The Angel which redeemed me from all evil, bless the lads; and let my name be named on them, and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac; and let them grow into a multitude in the midst of the earth."}, facts:["Did you know Jacob adopted Joseph's two sons as his own, saying, as Reuben and Simeon, they shall be mine?","Did you know Jacob crossed his hands on purpose, laying his right hand on the younger son, Ephraim?","Did you know Jacob's eyes were dim with age, yet he kissed and embraced grandsons he could barely see?"], questions:[
{q:"Whom did Joseph take with him when he heard his father was sick?",options:["His two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim","His brothers Judah and Reuben","His wife Asenath and her servants","The physicians of Pharaoh"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:1",verse:"And it came to pass after these things, that one told Joseph, Behold, thy father is sick: and he took with him his two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim.",insight:"Joseph brought his two sons to the sickbed. Bringing the next generation to receive blessing is a father's wisdom."},
{q:"What did Israel do when he heard Joseph was coming?",options:["Strengthened himself and sat upon the bed","Rose and walked to meet him","Called all his sons together","Wept and covered his face"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:2",verse:"And one told Jacob, and said, Behold, thy son Joseph cometh unto thee: and Israel strengthened himself, and sat upon the bed.",insight:"The dying patriarch gathered his strength to sit up. Blessing others can summon strength we thought was gone."},
{q:"Where did Jacob say God Almighty had appeared to him?",options:["At Luz in the land of Canaan","At Padanaram in Mesopotamia","At Shechem by the oak","At Hebron in the valley"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:3",verse:"And Jacob said unto Joseph, God Almighty appeared unto me at Luz in the land of Canaan, and blessed me,",insight:"Jacob remembered Luz, where God first blessed him. Old encounters with God fuel present faith."},
{q:"What did God promise to give Jacob's seed?",options:["This land for an everlasting possession","The riches of Egypt forever","A kingdom above all nations","The rivers and the seas"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:4",verse:"And said unto me, Behold, I will make thee fruitful, and multiply thee, and I will make of thee a multitude of people; and will give this land to thy seed after thee for an everlasting possession.",insight:"An everlasting possession of land was promised to his seed. God's gifts to His people are built to last."},
{q:"As whom did Jacob claim Ephraim and Manasseh?",options:["As Reuben and Simeon","As Judah and Levi","As Dan and Naphtali","As Gad and Asher"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:5",verse:"And now thy two sons, Ephraim and Manasseh, which were born unto thee in the land of Egypt before I came unto thee into Egypt, are mine; as Reuben and Simeon, they shall be mine.",insight:"Jacob adopted the grandsons as his own sons, as Reuben and Simeon. Adoption into the family is God's own pattern."},
{q:"Where did Jacob say Rachel died and was buried?",options:["In the way of Ephrath, the same is Bethlehem","At Hebron in the cave of Machpelah","By the well of Beersheba","At Shechem under the oak"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:7",verse:"And as for me, when I came from Padan, Rachel died by me in the land of Canaan in the way, when yet there was but a little way to come unto Ephrath: and I buried her there in the way of Ephrath; the same is Bethlehem.",insight:"Rachel died on the road to Ephrath, and Jacob never forgot. Love keeps its memorials across the decades."},
{q:"What did Israel ask when Joseph brought his sons near?",options:["Who are these?","Whence come they?","What are their names?","Are they thy sons?"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:8",verse:"And Israel beheld Joseph’s sons, and said, Who are these?",insight:"His dim eyes could not tell, so he asked, Who are these? Asking plainly is better than blessing blindly."},
{q:"Why could Israel not see Joseph's sons clearly?",options:["His eyes were dim for age","The tent was dark at evening","His sons stood far away","Tears clouded his vision"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:10",verse:"Now the eyes of Israel were dim for age, so that he could not see. And he brought them near unto him; and he kissed them, and embraced them.",insight:"Age had dimmed his eyes, but not his discernment. Spiritual sight can sharpen as physical sight fades."},
{q:"What did Israel do when the lads were brought near to him?",options:["Kissed them and embraced them","Laid his staff upon them","Anointed them with oil","Lifted them onto his knees"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:10",verse:"Now the eyes of Israel were dim for age, so that he could not see. And he brought them near unto him; and he kissed them, and embraced them.",insight:"He kissed and embraced grandsons he could barely see. Affection does not require clear sight, only a full heart."},
{q:"What had Jacob never thought he would see again?",options:["Joseph's face","The land of Canaan","His brother Esau","The stars of heaven"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:11",verse:"And Israel said unto Joseph, I had not thought to see thy face: and, lo, God hath shewed me also thy seed.",insight:"I had not thought to see thy face, he said, and God showed him his seed too. God exceeds our smallest hopes."},
{q:"How did Joseph place his sons before Israel?",options:["Ephraim toward Israel's left hand, Manasseh toward his right","Both sons directly before his face","Ephraim at his feet, Manasseh at his side","Manasseh toward Israel's left, Ephraim toward his right"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:13",verse:"And Joseph took them both, Ephraim in his right hand toward Israel’s left hand, and Manasseh in his left hand toward Israel’s right hand, and brought them near unto him.",insight:"Joseph arranged them carefully, firstborn to the right hand. Thoughtful preparation honors both father and sons."},
{q:"Upon whose head did Israel lay his right hand?",options:["Ephraim's, though he was the younger","Manasseh's, for he was the firstborn","Both lads' at once","Neither, until Joseph agreed"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:14",verse:"And Israel stretched out his right hand, and laid it upon Ephraim’s head, who was the younger, and his left hand upon Manasseh’s head, guiding his hands wittingly; for Manasseh was the firstborn.",insight:"The right hand of blessing fell on the younger, Ephraim. God is not bound by birth order or human custom."},
{q:"How did Israel guide his hands when he crossed them?",options:["Wittingly, knowing what he did","Trembling, by mistake","Blindly, without knowing","Slowly, seeking Joseph's leave"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:14",verse:"And Israel stretched out his right hand, and laid it upon Ephraim’s head, who was the younger, and his left hand upon Manasseh’s head, guiding his hands wittingly; for Manasseh was the firstborn.",insight:"He guided his hands wittingly. What looked like confusion was deliberate obedience to God's choice."},
{q:"Before whom did Jacob say his fathers Abraham and Isaac had walked?",options:["God","The angels of heaven","The kings of Canaan","The elders of the land"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:15",verse:"And he blessed Joseph, and said, God, before whom my fathers Abraham and Isaac did walk, the God which fed me all my life long unto this day,",insight:"God, before whom my fathers walked, had fed Jacob all his life. A lifetime of provision deserves a lifetime of praise."},
{q:"Whom did Jacob call upon to bless the lads?",options:["The Angel which redeemed me from all evil","The God of the mountains","The Lord of the harvest","The Keeper of Israel's tents"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:16",verse:"The Angel which redeemed me from all evil, bless the lads; and let my name be named on them, and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac; and let them grow into a multitude in the midst of the earth.",insight:"The Angel who redeemed him from all evil would bless the boys. The redeemed become channels of blessing."},
{q:"What displeased Joseph during the blessing?",options:["His father laid his right hand on Ephraim's head","Jacob blessed the lads before blessing him","The blessing was spoken in Canaan's tongue","His sons were adopted as Jacob's own"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:17",verse:"And when Joseph saw that his father laid his right hand upon the head of Ephraim, it displeased him: and he held up his father’s hand, to remove it from Ephraim’s head unto Manasseh’s head.",insight:"Joseph tried to move his father's hand to the firstborn. Even good sons can resist God's surprising choices."},
{q:"What did Joseph ask his father to do?",options:["Put thy right hand upon Manasseh's head, the firstborn","Bless him before the lads","Speak the blessing twice over","Lay both hands on both sons"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:18",verse:"And Joseph said unto his father, Not so, my father: for this is the firstborn; put thy right hand upon his head.",insight:"Not so, my father, Joseph pleaded for the firstborn's right. Custom is strong, but God's purpose is stronger."},
{q:"What did Jacob prophesy concerning the younger brother?",options:["He shall be greater, and his seed a multitude of nations","He shall serve his elder all his days","He shall return to dwell in Canaan","He shall be a priest unto his brethren"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:19",verse:"And his father refused, and said, I know it, my son, I know it: he also shall become a people, and he also shall be great: but truly his younger brother shall be greater than he, and his seed shall become a multitude of nations.",insight:"The younger would be greater, his seed a multitude of nations. God's election lifts whom He wills."},
{q:"In what words would Israel bless in days to come?",options:["God make thee as Ephraim and as Manasseh","The Lord lift up His countenance upon thee","Blessed be the God of Abraham and Isaac","May thy seed possess the gates of enemies"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:20",verse:"And he blessed them that day, saying, In thee shall Israel bless, saying, God make thee as Ephraim and as Manasseh: and he set Ephraim before Manasseh.",insight:"God make thee as Ephraim and as Manasseh became Israel's blessing. Transformed lives become the standard of blessing."},
{q:"What did Israel say God would do for Joseph's family after his death?",options:["Be with them and bring them again to the land of their fathers","Multiply them as the stars in Egypt","Make them rulers over Pharaoh's house","Give them the land of Goshen forever"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 48:21",verse:"And Israel said unto Joseph, Behold, I die: but God shall be with you, and bring you again unto the land of your fathers.",insight:"Behold, I die, but God shall be with you. Leaders pass; God's presence remains with His people."}
]},
{n:49, name:"The Twelve Tribes Blessed", seal:{ref:"Genesis 49:10",verse:"The sceptre shall not depart from Judah, nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be."}, facts:["Did you know Jacob's blessing of Judah holds one of Scripture's great promises, that the sceptre shall not depart from Judah until Shiloh come?","Did you know Jacob charged his sons to bury him in the cave of Machpelah, where Abraham, Sarah, Isaac, Rebekah, and Leah already rested?","Did you know that when Jacob finished commanding his sons, he gathered up his feet into the bed and yielded up the ghost?"], questions:[
{q:"Why did Jacob call his sons together at the end of his life?",options:["To tell them what shall befall them in the last days","To divide his flocks among them","To appoint Judah as their king","To send them back to Canaan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:1",verse:"And Jacob called unto his sons, and said, Gather yourselves together, that I may tell you that which shall befall you in the last days.",insight:"He gathered them to speak of the last days. A father's final words should point his children toward God's future."},
{q:"How is Reuben described as Jacob's firstborn?",options:["My might, the beginning of my strength, the excellency of dignity and power","My beloved, the joy of my youth, the pride of my house","My strong one, the lion of my tribe, the keeper of my tents","My eldest, the heir of my flocks, the ruler of my house"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:3",verse:"Reuben, thou art my firstborn, my might, and the beginning of my strength, the excellency of dignity, and the excellency of power:",insight:"Reuben held the excellency of dignity as firstborn. Privilege is real, but it must be kept with character."},
{q:"Why would Reuben not excel?",options:["He was unstable as water and defiled his father's bed","He refused to go down into Egypt","He sold his birthright for bread","He worshipped the gods of Canaan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:4",verse:"Unstable as water, thou shalt not excel; because thou wentest up to thy father’s bed; then defiledst thou it: he went up to my couch.",insight:"Unstable as water, Reuben lost the excellency through sin. Gifts without steadiness cannot lead."},
{q:"Which two brothers are called instruments of cruelty?",options:["Simeon and Levi","Reuben and Judah","Dan and Naphtali","Issachar and Zebulun"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:5",verse:"Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations.",insight:"Simeon and Levi's anger made them cruel. Zeal without love becomes an instrument of harm."},
{q:"What did Jacob decree for Simeon and Levi?",options:["I will divide them in Jacob and scatter them in Israel","They shall dwell apart beyond the river","Their inheritance shall be taken by Judah","They shall serve the other tribes forever"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:7",verse:"Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce; and their wrath, for it was cruel: I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Israel.",insight:"Their fierce anger would scatter them in Israel. Uncontrolled wrath forfeits a settled inheritance."},
{q:"What did Jacob say Judah's brethren would do?",options:["Praise him","Serve him","Fear him","Follow him"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:8",verse:"Judah, thou art he whom thy brethren shall praise: thy hand shall be in the neck of thine enemies; thy father’s children shall bow down before thee.",insight:"Thou art he whom thy brethren shall praise. True leadership earns praise rather than demanding it."},
{q:"To what animal is Judah likened?",options:["A lion's whelp","A young bull","A swift hart","A strong eagle"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:9",verse:"Judah is a lion’s whelp: from the prey, my son, thou art gone up: he stooped down, he couched as a lion, and as an old lion; who shall rouse him up?",insight:"Judah is a lion's whelp, couched and fearless. From this tribe would come the Lion who needs no rousing."},
{q:"What shall not depart from Judah, according to Jacob's blessing?",options:["The sceptre, nor a lawgiver, until Shiloh come","The sword, nor the shield, until the end","The crown, nor the tribute, forever","The altar, nor the priesthood, always"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:10",verse:"The sceptre shall not depart from Judah, nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.",insight:"The sceptre would stay with Judah until Shiloh come. Kingship was heading somewhere, to Someone."},
{q:"How are Judah's eyes and teeth described in the blessing?",options:["Eyes red with wine, teeth white with milk","Eyes bright with joy, teeth strong as flint","Eyes keen as eagles, teeth white as snow","Eyes deep as wells, teeth sharp as swords"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:12",verse:"His eyes shall be red with wine, and his teeth white with milk.",insight:"Red eyes with wine and white teeth with milk picture abundance. Judah's portion would overflow with good."},
{q:"Where shall Zebulun dwell?",options:["At the haven of the sea, a haven of ships, his border unto Zidon","In the hill country of Ephraim","By the brook of Egypt","In the valley of Jezreel"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:13",verse:"Zebulun shall dwell at the haven of the sea; and he shall be for an haven of ships; and his border shall be unto Zidon.",insight:"Zebulun would dwell by the sea with ships. Each tribe had its place appointed by the father's word."},
{q:"To what is Issachar likened?",options:["A strong ass couching down between two burdens","A fleet horse running the plain","A patient ox at the plow","A burdened camel on the road"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:14",verse:"Issachar is a strong ass couching down between two burdens:",insight:"Issachar the strong ass bowed his shoulder to bear. Strength finds its purpose in willing service."},
{q:"What shall Dan do among the tribes?",options:["Judge his people, as one of the tribes of Israel","Lead the armies into battle","Keep the records of the tribes","Guard the borders of the land"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:16",verse:"Dan shall judge his people, as one of the tribes of Israel.",insight:"Dan shall judge his people. Even a small tribe carries the high calling of justice."},
{q:"To what is Dan likened in Jacob's blessing?",options:["A serpent by the way, an adder in the path","A wolf among the sheep","A scorpion in the sand","A viper in the rocks"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:17",verse:"Dan shall be a serpent by the way, an adder in the path, that biteth the horse heels, so that his rider shall fall backward.",insight:"Dan the serpent bites the horse's heels. Small and hidden can still overthrow the mighty rider."},
{q:"What is said of Gad in the blessing?",options:["A troop shall overcome him, but he shall overcome at the last","He shall dwell in safety all his days","His enemies shall flee before him","He shall never see battle"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:19",verse:"Gad, a troop shall overcome him: but he shall overcome at the last.",insight:"A troop would overcome Gad, but he would overcome at the last. Defeat is not the end for those who endure."},
{q:"What shall Asher yield?",options:["Royal dainties, for his bread shall be fat","Fine oil for the lamps","Sweet honey from the rock","Strong wine for the king"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:20",verse:"Out of Asher his bread shall be fat, and he shall yield royal dainties.",insight:"Out of Asher would come royal dainties. God gives some a portion fit for kings' tables."},
{q:"To what is Naphtali likened?",options:["A hind let loose, giving goodly words","A dove returning with an olive leaf","A nightingale singing at dawn","A gazelle leaping on the hills"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:21",verse:"Naphtali is a hind let loose: he giveth goodly words.",insight:"Naphtali the hind let loose gives goodly words. Freedom of spirit produces beautiful speech."},
{q:"How is Joseph described in his father's blessing?",options:["A fruitful bough by a well, whose branches run over the wall","A cedar of Lebanon, tall and strong","A palm tree flourishing in the desert","An olive tree full of oil"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:22",verse:"Joseph is a fruitful bough, even a fruitful bough by a well; whose branches run over the wall:",insight:"Joseph the fruitful bough drew from the well and spread over the wall. Deep roots produce wide influence."},
{q:"Who sorely grieved Joseph, according to the blessing?",options:["The archers, who shot at him and hated him","The Midianites, who sold him for silver","The taskmasters, who burdened him","The magicians, who opposed him"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:23",verse:"The archers have sorely grieved him, and shot at him, and hated him:",insight:"The archers shot at him and hated him, yet his bow abode in strength. Attacked on every side, the faithful endure."},
{q:"To what is Benjamin likened?",options:["A wolf that ravens, devouring prey in the morning and dividing spoil at night","A lion roaring for its prey","A bear robbed of her whelps","A leopard watching by night"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:27",verse:"Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil.",insight:"Benjamin the wolf devours in the morning and divides at night. Fierceness has its place in God's family too."},
{q:"In which cave did Jacob command his sons to bury him?",options:["The cave in the field of Machpelah, before Mamre","The cave of Adullam in Judah","A tomb in the valley of Shechem","The sepulchre of Rachel at Ephrath"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 49:30",verse:"In the cave that is in the field of Machpelah, which is before Mamre, in the land of Canaan, which Abraham bought with the field of Ephron the Hittite for a possession of a buryingplace.",insight:"Machpelah, bought by Abraham, would hold Jacob too. The patriarchs rest together, awaiting the promise."}
]},
{n:50, name:"God Meant It unto Good", seal:{ref:"Genesis 50:20",verse:"But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but God meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive."}, facts:["Did you know the Egyptians mourned Jacob for seventy days, and his funeral train went up with chariots and horsemen, a very great company?","Did you know the Canaanites named the mourning place Abelmizraim, meaning the mourning of the Egyptians?","Did you know Joseph lived to see his great-grandchildren, the third generation of Ephraim, and died at 110 years old?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Joseph do when his father died?",options:["Fell upon his face, wept upon him, and kissed him","Rent his clothes and sat in ashes","Called the elders to lament","Covered his face and went apart"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:1",verse:"And Joseph fell upon his father’s face, and wept upon him, and kissed him.",insight:"Joseph fell on his father's face and wept. The ruler of Egypt was first a grieving son."},
{q:"Whom did Joseph command to embalm his father?",options:["His servants the physicians","The priests of On","The elders of Egypt","The midwives of Goshen"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:2",verse:"And Joseph commanded his servants the physicians to embalm his father: and the physicians embalmed Israel.",insight:"Physicians embalmed Israel at Joseph's command. Honor for parents uses every skill at hand."},
{q:"How long did the Egyptians mourn for Jacob?",options:["Threescore and ten days","Forty days","Seven days","Thirty days"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:3",verse:"And forty days were fulfilled for him; for so are fulfilled the days of those which are embalmed: and the Egyptians mourned for him threescore and ten days.",insight:"Seventy days of mourning honored the shepherd from Canaan. A life with God is honored even by strangers."},
{q:"What had Jacob made Joseph swear concerning his burial?",options:["Bury me in my grave which I have digged in the land of Canaan","Lay me in the Nile's waters","Build me a pyramid in Egypt","Burn my body with spices"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:5",verse:"My father made me swear, saying, Lo, I die: in my grave which I have digged for me in the land of Canaan, there shalt thou bury me. Now therefore let me go up, I pray thee, and bury my father, and I will come again.",insight:"Jacob had dug his own grave in Canaan and made Joseph swear. Hope plans ahead, even for burial."},
{q:"What did Pharaoh say when Joseph asked leave to bury his father?",options:["Go up, and bury thy father, according as he made thee swear","Send thy brothers, but remain thou here","Bury him in the royal sepulchre","Wait until the famine is ended"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:6",verse:"And Pharaoh said, Go up, and bury thy father, according as he made thee swear.",insight:"Pharaoh honored a son's oath to his father. Even kings respect covenant faithfulness."},
{q:"Who went up with Joseph to bury his father?",options:["All the servants of Pharaoh and the elders of Egypt","Only his eleven brothers","The priests and the army captains","The shepherds of Goshen alone"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:7",verse:"And Joseph went up to bury his father: and with him went up all the servants of Pharaoh, the elders of his house, and all the elders of the land of Egypt,",insight:"Egypt's elders walked with Joseph to Canaan. Godliness earns honor across every boundary."},
{q:"Who was left behind in the land of Goshen?",options:["Their little ones, their flocks, and their herds","The aged and the sick","The women and the servants","The cattle and the storehouses"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:8",verse:"And all the house of Joseph, and his brethren, and his father’s house: only their little ones, and their flocks, and their herds, they left in the land of Goshen.",insight:"Little ones and flocks stayed in Goshen. Life and livelihood went on even in the season of mourning."},
{q:"What made the funeral procession a very great company?",options:["Both chariots and horsemen went up with him","All the tribes of Canaan joined them","Pharaoh himself led the march","Thousands of mourners hired for the day"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:9",verse:"And there went up with him both chariots and horsemen: and it was a very great company.",insight:"Chariots and horsemen honored a shepherd's burial. God exalts the humble in ways no one expects."},
{q:"Where did they mourn seven days for Jacob?",options:["At the threshingfloor of Atad, beyond Jordan","In the field of Machpelah","At the brook of Eshcol","In the plain of Mamre"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:10",verse:"And they came to the threshingfloor of Atad, which is beyond Jordan, and there they mourned with a great and very sore lamentation: and he made a mourning for his father seven days.",insight:"Seven days of sore lamentation at Atad's threshingfloor. Grief deserves its full measure, not a hurried farewell."},
{q:"What did the Canaanites call the place of mourning?",options:["Abelmizraim","Mamre","Beersheba","Gilgal"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:11",verse:"And when the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, saw the mourning in the floor of Atad, they said, This is a grievous mourning to the Egyptians: wherefore the name of it was called Abel-mizraim, which is beyond Jordan.",insight:"They named it Abelmizraim, the mourning of the Egyptians. Witnesses name what they see; let them see genuine grief and honor."},
{q:"Where was Jacob finally buried?",options:["In the cave of the field of Machpelah, before Mamre","In a pyramid near the Nile","In the royal tombs of Thebes","In the field of Ephron at Shechem"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:13",verse:"For his sons carried him into the land of Canaan, and buried him in the cave of the field of Machpelah, which Abraham bought with the field for a possession of a buryingplace of Ephron the Hittite, before Mamre.",insight:"His sons carried him to Machpelah, as he commanded. Promises to the dying are sacred trusts."},
{q:"What did Joseph's brothers fear after their father died?",options:["Joseph would hate them and requite the evil they did","Pharaoh would enslave them all","The Egyptians would drive them out","Famine would return to the land"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:15",verse:"And when Joseph’s brethren saw that their father was dead, they said, Joseph will peradventure hate us, and will certainly requite us all the evil which we did unto him.",insight:"With Jacob gone, old guilt resurfaced. Unforgiven fear outlives the circumstances that made it."},
{q:"What message did the brothers send to Joseph?",options:["Thy father commanded: forgive the trespass of thy brethren","Our father left thee his blessing alone","Pharaoh requires thy presence at court","The famine has returned to Canaan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:17",verse:"So shall ye say unto Joseph, Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil: and now, we pray thee, forgive the trespass of the servants of the God of thy father. And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.",insight:"They sent word that their father had pled for their forgiveness. The humble ask; pride never does."},
{q:"What did Joseph do when the brothers' message reached him?",options:["He wept","He grew angry","He sent them away","He called Pharaoh's guard"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:17",verse:"So shall ye say unto Joseph, Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil: and now, we pray thee, forgive the trespass of the servants of the God of thy father. And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.",insight:"Joseph wept when they spoke. Tender hearts forgive; hard hearts keep accounts."},
{q:"What did the brothers do when they came before Joseph?",options:["Fell down before his face and said, We be thy servants","Offered him gifts of silver and gold","Knelt and asked for land in Goshen","Stood silent and waited his word"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:18",verse:"And his brethren also went and fell down before his face; and they said, Behold, we be thy servants.",insight:"They fell down, saying, We be thy servants. The old dreams were fulfilled in an hour of mercy, not revenge."},
{q:"How did Joseph answer his fearful brothers?",options:["Fear not: for am I in the place of God?","Depart from me, ye workers of evil","Bring me proof of your repentance","Serve me seven years for your sin"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:19",verse:"And Joseph said unto them, Fear not: for am I in the place of God?",insight:"Am I in the place of God? Joseph refused the seat of judgment. Forgiveness leaves vengeance to the Lord."},
{q:"What did Joseph say God had meant for good?",options:["The evil his brothers thought against him, to save much people alive","The famine, to enrich Pharaoh's storehouses","His prison years, to humble the Egyptians","Their journey, to settle them in Goshen"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:20",verse:"But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but God meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.",insight:"Ye thought evil against me, but God meant it unto good. The worst human intentions become raw material for divine mercy."},
{q:"What did Joseph promise his brothers and their little ones?",options:["I will nourish you","I will make you rulers","I will send you back to Canaan","I will divide my riches among you"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:21",verse:"Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.",insight:"I will nourish you, he said, and comforted them kindly. Forgiveness feeds; it does not merely pardon."},
{q:"How old was Joseph when he died?",options:["An hundred and ten years","An hundred and twenty years","An hundred and forty years","Ninety and three years"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:22",verse:"And Joseph dwelt in Egypt, he, and his father’s house: and Joseph lived an hundred and ten years.",insight:"Joseph lived 110 years, long enough to see the third generation. Faithfulness compounds across generations."},
{q:"What oath did Joseph take of the children of Israel before he died?",options:["Ye shall carry up my bones from hence when God visits you","Ye shall never return to Canaan","Ye shall serve Pharaoh all your days","Ye shall bury me in the Nile"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 50:25",verse:"And Joseph took an oath of the children of Israel, saying, God will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.",insight:"Carry up my bones, he charged them. Joseph died believing the exodus before it happened; faith sees the promise fulfilled."}
]}
]);
